µï,ó"*L2t Só(ù8ïaVbëTªò/ÑL~K√€{"rendered":{"html":"<p>You can share a type and helper across files by putting them in a\nworkspace. This example gives the entry file access to root declarations\nwithout an import.</p>\n<h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#before-you-start\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>You need <code>gcsl</code> on your command search path and an empty writable directory.</p>\n<h2 id=\"create-the-workspace\">Create the workspace <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#create-the-workspace\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Save these declarations as <code>workspace.gcsl</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\" data-language=\"gcsl\"><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\" data-copy-code><span class=\"copy-label\">Copy</span></button><pre><code>type Component = {name: String, version: String}\ndef describe(item: Component): String {\n    \"{item.name} {item.version}\"\n}\n</code></pre></div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Save the entry program as <code>main.gcsl</code> beside it:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\" data-language=\"gcsl\"><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\" data-copy-code><span class=\"copy-label\">Copy</span></button><pre><code>describe({name = \"gcsl\"; version = \"0.1.0\"})\n</code></pre></div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>From that directory, check the workspace and run the entry file:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\" data-copy-code><span class=\"copy-label\">Copy</span></button><pre><code><span class=\"hl-source hl-shell hl-bash\"><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-shell\"><span class=\"hl-variable hl-function hl-shell\">gcsl</span></span><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell\"> check</span>\n<span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-shell\"><span class=\"hl-variable hl-function hl-shell\">gcsl</span></span><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell\"> run main.gcsl</span>\n</span></code></pre></div>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"check-the-result\">Check the result <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#check-the-result\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The check reports <code>no problems in 2 files checked</code>. The run prints\n<code>gcsl 0.1.0</code>. The helper is visible because <code>def</code> contributes to the\nshared directory scope. Replacing <code>def</code> with <code>fn</code> makes it private to\n<code>workspace.gcsl</code>, so the entry file cannot resolve it.</p>\n<p>When adding a child library directory, import its public fields or\nfunctions by its root-relative path. Keep independent projects behind\ntheir own workspace markers rather than relying on hidden files to\nseparate their scopes.</p>\n","toc":[{"level":2,"id":"before-you-start","title":"Before you start","number":null},{"level":2,"id":"create-the-workspace","title":"Create the workspace","number":null},{"level":2,"id":"check-the-result","title":"Check the result","number":null}],"has_mermaid":false,"dangling":[],"warnings":[],"broken":[]},"images":[],"links":{"pages":[],"anchors":[]},"refs":[]}